  "core": [
    {
      "section": "A2",
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "Appendix B Limitations and Future Directions."
    },
    {
      "section": "A2",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "First, the current study focuses on single-modal memory evolution, whereas real-world agents often operate over multimodal inputs. Extending TAME to support multimodal memory representations and cross-modal trustworthiness evaluation remains an important direction for future work."
    },
    {
      "section": "A2",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "Second, although TAME achieves improved overall trustworthiness during test-time learning, we observe that different learned strategies may exhibit heterogeneous behaviors across individual trust dimensions. A global decline in aggregated trustworthiness does not necessarily imply monotonic degradation in every specific property. Future work should therefore develop more fine-grained analytical paradigms to characterize dimension-wise trustworthiness dynamics."
    },
    {
      "section": "A2",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "Third, unlike approaches that rely on external prompt modifications or post-hoc safety guardrails, TAME is designed as an endogenous test-time learning paradigm that addresses memory misevolution from within the evolution mechanism itself. While effective, this paradigm can be further refined, and future work may explore more efficient internal optimization strategies, as well as selectively integrating lightweight training signals to further enhance robustness and performance."
    },
    {
      "section": "A4",
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "Appendix D Method Prompt."
    }
  ]
